            "fullText": "Milan for Trees Fund is a locally led trust fund managed by the municipality of Milan and is dedicated to tree planting in the city. The fund is capitalized through a blend of municipal tax revenues, individual contributions and larger corporate donations. The money is held off the municipal balance sheet, and the fund allows tree planting to extend beyond public land. In 2024, 600 citizens and 36 local business participated to raise over EUR 1.3 million to plant over 4700 trees. It is a good example of how a city can lead local multi-stakeholder partnerships, bringing in private capital to fund place-based climate action. The city of Lund in Sweden is also planning to replicate this model to accelerate municipal tree planting, which will not only improve local climatic conditions but also provide additional economic value to businesses through place-based improvements.",
