            "connectionLine": "Why see this: See how a creditworthy city can connect a portfolio of climate investments to capital markets through a green bond framework.",
            "excerpt": "Lund’s green bond programme is a strong example of a local climate finance structure showing how a city can translate climate priorities into a municipally anchored investment vehicle.",
            "fullText": "Lund’s green bond programme is a strong example of a local climate finance structure because it shows how a city can translate climate priorities into a municipally anchored investment vehicle. Lund began issuing green bonds in 2017, and by end-2025 had an outstanding green bond volume of USD 450 million. Lund municipality updated its green bonds framework, incorporating elements from the EU Taxonomy for sustainable investments, broadening the range of eligible projects. The framework also sets up how projects are selected, monitored and reported, and is used to connect investment planning with climate and sustainability goals while improving transparency and accountability to investors. The portfolio spans climate-smart infrastructure and buildings across the municipality and its wholly owned housing, parking and water utility companies, with examples such as the Lund tramway and the LKF housing project showing how the bond framework channels finance into a tracked green portfolio of approved projects.",
