            "connectionLine": "Why see this: See how guarantees and credit enhancement can reduce financing risks and mobilize domestic institutional capital.",
            "excerpt": "InfraCredit Nigeria is a strong example of how a local credit-enhancement facility can unlock domestic capital for infrastructure.",
            "fullText": "InfraCredit Nigeria is a strong example of how a local credit-enhancement facility can unlock domestic capital for infrastructure. Established in 2017 through a partnership between PIDG, GuarantCo and the Nigeria Sovereign Investment Authority, InfraCredit provides NGN-denominated guarantees that improve the credit quality of local-currency debt instruments and help projects access longer-tenor finance from institutional investors such as pension funds, insurers and banks that would otherwise not invest. By end-2024, it had guaranteed 24 transactions mobilising over NGN 200 billion in private investment, supported nearly NGN 150 billion in bond issuances, and helped first-time issuers such as North South Power access the domestic capital market. InfraCredit’s portfolio spans projects in Abuja, Lagos, Ondo, Imo, Abia, Cross River, Enugu, Bayelsa, Ado Ekiti and Victoria Island, including solar mini-grids, embedded power, housing, telecoms, a ring road and industrial infrastructure, showing how a national credit-enhancement vehicle can channel finance into a wide range of place-based investments.\n\nThe model has also been replicated beyond Nigeria through sister facilities in Pakistan, Kenya and Cambodia, with additional markets including Vietnam, Ghana and Francophone West Africa under development or review.",
