            "excerpt": "Kommuninvest is a locally led Swedish municipal aggregation mechanism that pools borrowing demand from municipalities and regions, giving them access to capital on more favourable terms.",
            "fullText": "Kommuninvest is a locally led Swedish municipal aggregation mechanism that pools borrowing demand from municipalities and regions, giving them access to capital on more favourable terms. It raises money in the market and on-lends it to its members, operating as a lending-only institution rather than a grant fund or equity vehicle. The model is backed by a joint guarantee from its 282 municipal and 15 regional members, which helps de-risk lending and lower borrowing costs. In 2025, Kommuninvest’s total lending reached SEK 563.9 billion, showing the scale that pooled municipal finance can achieve.",
