                "excerpt": "CCFLA’s Brazil Local Hub works as a place-based implementation platform that brings together 50 local, national and global partners...",
                "fullText": "CCFLA’s Brazil Local Hub works as a place-based implementation platform that brings together 50 local, national and global partners to help cities facing floods, droughts and infrastructure gaps move from fragmented demand to more coordinated urban climate action. Rather than operating as a stand-alone convening effort, it is built around two implementation-oriented initiatives: a community-of-practice that aligns actors and accelerates implementation, and the PCVR Project Bank, co-developed with Brazil’s Ministry of the Environment, which maps subnational urban projects at different stages so they can be matched more effectively with technical assistance, funding and finance.",
